title:: BMControllerAutomatorGUI
summary:: Documentation BEASTmulch - GUI for a BMControllerAutomator
categories:: Classes

Description::

This is a GUI class for link::Classes/Automation/BMControllerAutomator::. It allows one to create or edit sequences and snapshots, and shows a visual representation of the automator's time base, for instance a soundfile graph.

See also: link::Classes/Automation/BMControllerAutomator::

CLASSMETHODS::

methods:: new
Create a new BMControllerAutomatorGUI.

argument:: ca
An instance of BMControllerAutomator.

argument:: name
A String indicating what to display in the title bar of the resulting window. The default is "Soundfile / Controller Snapshots".

argument:: origin
A Point indicating the origin of the resulting window. The default is 200@200.



Examples::

code::
s.boot;

(
// a source and time reference
p = BMSoundFilePlayer(name:\bar);
p.read("sounds/a11wlk01.wav");
)

(
// make a speaker list
l = [[-30, 'L'], [30, 'R'], [0, 'C'], [-110, 'Ls'], [110, 'Rs']].collectAs({|el, i|
	BMSpeaker.newFromSpherical(el[1], i, el[0], 0, 2);
}, BMInOutArray);

m = BMAudioMatrix(p, l, name:'Router'); // make a matrix for connections
m.connect('bar-1', l.keys);

// a controller to automate and an amp control matrix
c = BMVirtualController(\foo, s, 5);
BMVirtualControllerSliders(c); // slider gui
n = BMAmpControlMatrix(c, m);
c.controlNames.do({|name, i| n.connect(name, l.keys[i])});

a = BMControllerAutomator(c.controlNames, p); // control virt sliders, player as time ref

// make a sequence and add some snapshots
c.setAllValues(0 ! 5);
a.addSequence('test1', 0, c.controlNames);
c.setVal(1, 0.5);
a.addSnapShot('test1', 0.5, 'test1-2');
c.setVal(2, 1);
a.addSnapShot('test1', 1, 'test1-3');
c.setAllValues({1.0.rand} ! 5);
a.addSnapShot('test1', 3, 'test1-4');
)

p.play.rate_(0.5); // half speed

BMControllerAutomatorGUI(a, origin: 100@600); // try out the GUI
::